PdfCraft VAIO preview

Open PdfCraft (VAIO preview) from Office or VAIO App Launcher, or open a PDF
with it through the file manager. Use Open, the page organizer and comment
tools; Save As preserves a separate copy. pdfcraft-vaio-cli exposes the
upstream headless tools. Application updates use APT and the existing
Check & Install Updates frontend, rather than upstream release downloads.

Measured on the Atom VAIO with an original three-page PDF: viewing,
render-to-PNG, text extraction, extracting/combining pages, page rotation,
and saved comments passed. Form creation/filling, applied redaction, an AES-256
password round trip and one-page image OCR also passed. Physical printing, digital signatures, advanced
forms and large scanned PDFs were not verified.
Those upstream features are retained; they are not compatibility promises.
The two hash-verified Ocrs models are included, under CC-BY-SA-4.0. OCR is
English/Latin-focused and CPU-intensive; the small single-page check passed.

This build selects OpenGL/Glow because the VAIO has no Vulkan support, and its
initial window fits the VAIO display. Native PDF Save As fills a missing .pdf
extension and asks before replacing an existing normalized destination.
It includes a private libxcb, upstream crypto unchanged, and upstream
permissive font/icon notices. The optional craft-fonts build input is absent,
so Japanese PDF text authoring is unavailable in this build.
The original ArtCraft trademark graphics were replaced by plain text labels.
No control server or MCP server is started by the package.

Removal: sudo apt-get remove pdfcraft-vaio (documents/settings are retained).
